ManSection.Description:
returns the fusion system on the pc group S generated by
Inn(S), the automorphisms in the list autSgens (or the
group autSgens of automorphisms of S), and the automorphisms
in essautos[i] of the subgroup essentials[i]
of S.

gap> S := ExtraspecialGroup( 27, 3 );;
gap> E := First( MaximalSubgroups( S ), M -> IsElementaryAbelian( M ) );;
gap> A := AutomorphismGroup( E );;  n := NiceMonomorphism( A );;
gap> sl := List( GeneratorsOfGroup( DerivedSubgroup( Image( n ) ) ),
>                x -> PreImagesRepresentative( n, x ) );;
gap> F := FusionSystem( S, [], [ E ], [ sl ] );
<fusion system on a group of order 3^3 with 1 essential classes>
gap> IsSaturated( F );
false

the list of all F-conjugates of P; whether P and
Q are F-conjugate; an isomorphism P \to Q in
F (or fail).

gap> F := GroupFusionSystem( PSL( 3, 4 ), 2 );;
gap> S := UnderlyingGroup( F );;
gap> cls := Filtered( List( ConjugacyClassesSubgroups( S ), Representative ), P -> Size( P ) = 2 );;
gap> Length( cls );  Length( FConjugacyClass( F, cls[1] ) );
9
63
gap> Size( AutF( F, UnderlyingGroup( F ) ) ) / Index( S, Center( S ) );
3

the usual properties of a subgroup P of S in F:
C_S(Q) \le Q for all F-conjugates Q of P;
|N_S(P)| (resp. |C_S(P)|) is maximal in the F-class;
Aut_S(P) is a Sylow p-subgroup of Aut_F(P);
O_p(Aut_F(P)) = Inn(P); P is fully automized and has the
surjectivity property; for all P < V \le N_S(P) the automorphisms
of P extending to F-automorphisms of V are exactly
the elements of Aut_F(P) normalizing Aut_V(P).

whether the fusion system F is saturated; the second function
returns [ true ] or [ false, reason ].  The test is the one
described in Chapter .  The essential subgroups of
F are required to be F-centric and fully normalized (for
the fusion system to be saturated with these essential subgroups); if
this fails the result is false.

gap> F := GroupFusionSystem( PSL( 3, 3 ), 3 );;
gap> FS_IsSaturatedWithReason( F );
[ true ]
gap> S := UnderlyingGroup( F );;
gap> F1 := FusionSystem( S, [], [ EssentialSubgroups( F )[1] ], [ EssentialAutomizers( F )[1] ] );;
gap> FS_IsSaturatedWithReason( F1 );
[ false, "the surjectivity property fails at a subgroup of order 9" ]

whether there is an isomorphism \alpha: S_1 \to S_2 carrying
F1 onto F2, i.e. carrying the generating data of F1
into F2 and vice versa; the second function returns such an
isomorphism or fail.  If F1 and F2 live on the same
group S, \alpha is searched in Aut(S); otherwise an
isomorphism of the groups is computed first.

gap> F1 := GroupFusionSystem( PSL( 3, 3 ), 3 );;
gap> F2 := GroupFusionSystem( MathieuGroup( 12 ), 3 );;
gap> IsIsomorphicFusionSystems( F1, F2 );
false
